{"ts":"2026-07-31T06:38:29.315Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"66076e2c28cfb4fafc6fb839","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-rl-mpd9"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Metric series live in item history, never in an item body"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"A run emits a monotonically growing series of metric events. Written to an item body, which is a scalar field, two concurrent writers produce a genuine conflict on every write, and a conflicted body is unparseable. Written to the append-only history stream, both sides' events survive a merge as their union, which pm-vcs proved empirically against a real git merge rather than by assumption. This single rule is what makes concurrent sweeps merge cleanly, so it is a constraint on every command that records a metric, not a convention."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Decision"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-31T06:38:29.315Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-31T06:38:29.315Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"No command writes a metric value to an item body or any scalar field; a test merges two branches that both logged to one run and asserts the union of events with zero conflicts and zero loss"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"b603d1c16cc586de57eb27f2fdefc23b55758010e10a5398d9dd0700234220cf","message":""}
